The eXpress Data Path: Fast Programmable Packet Processing in the OS Kernel (Høiland-Jørgensen et al., 2018)
Method: Runs eBPF bytecode in the network driver before kernel memory allocation.
Dataset: Linux routing & DDoS benchmarks.
Advantages: Processes up to 24 million packets per second per core.
Limitations: Primarily used for simple packet dropping and firewalling.
Research Gap: Adapting XDP for active, application-aware QoS scheduling.
Possible Improvements: Uses XDP as an active QoS router to prioritize UDP game traffic and trigger AI state fixes.
